# Repos the regtest-miner suite needs checked out BESIDE it on the CI venue.
#
# Declaring a sibling here is what makes its cross-repo guards actually run. An
# UNdeclared sibling is not a neutral omission: test/unit/coins-conformance.test.js
# skips its byte-identity half via existsSync when ../xchain-hub is absent
# rather than failing, so a gate that let this sibling go missing would still
# print PASS having exercised none of that guard. The GitHub drift-guards job
# (.github/workflows/ci.yml) also checks out xchain-hub to run
# xchain-hub/bin/sync-coins.sh --check against this repo.
#
# ci-dispatch.sh ships each of these at its origin/master (falling back to local
# HEAD) and REFUSES the push if one is not a checkout beside this repo, so a
# declared sibling can never be silently absent.

# Vendored coins-registry byte-identity (BTC/LTC/DOGE/index/consensus_pin) and
# the sync-coins.sh drift check the GitHub drift-guards job runs.
xchain-hub
